Package: [[package.name]]
# Not [[version]]: that is the raw Maven version, and apt compares on this line. This is the planner's version with
# -SNAPSHOT rewritten to ~snapshot.<run>, which sorts below the release rather than above it.
Version: [[planner.package.version]]
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Michael Schnell <michael@fuin.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/porelo-ai/porelo-planner
# The native executable links against both; jdeb does not read it to find out. check-linkage holds these floors to it.
Depends: libc6 (>= [[package.glibc.floor]]), zlib1g (>= 1:[[package.zlib.floor]])
Description: Porelo's planner: a project's stories and issues for the Porelo window
 Serves a project's stories and issues to the Porelo window over a REST API on
 the loopback address, and writes their state changes to the planning store in
 Git with the person's own login. Installs into /usr/libexec/porelo as
 'planner', where the window finds it and starts it as it needs it.
